{"repositoryId":1411206631,"availability":"available","full":"ibs-CMG-NGS/fig-atlas","name":"fig-atlas","description":"Config-driven, verifiable and provenance-tracked publication figures across a paper's lifecycle","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T02:59:36Z","updated":"2026-10-13T02:09:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ibs-cmg-ngs.github.io/fig-atlas/","topics":[],"demo":"https://ibs-cmg-ngs.github.io/fig-atlas/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.138Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.138Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.138Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.138Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Config-driven, verifiable and provenance-tracked publication figures — across a paper's lifecycle.","fig-atlas is a layer above matplotlib for the figures of a scientific paper. Each figure is a reproducible build product of a data bundle, a commented configuration and a renderer:","comment giving its role, unit and how to tune it. Researchers change figures without reading code."],"features":["Every visual value lives in the config — colours, sizes, thresholds, layout — each with a","Figures are drawn at final print size (1:1 on page presets) and checked before print:","Every figure records its provenance — the data files it actually read (with hashes), the","Numbers, statistics and images stay honest: legend numbers are filled from the analysis,","The paper's storyline is a ledger: which project is Main Figure N, numbered revision records"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ibs-CMG-NGS/fig-atlas/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a5f2a487b09ada1d150f6bb6922cff657dec1e46e5e2a7e2f9dc1a7665284624","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.396Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T02:12:44.396Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Config-driven, verifiable and provenance-track